---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import hiking from '../assets/images/hiking.jpg';

const photos = [{ src: hiking, alt: 'Hiking along a mountain trail' }];
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="A bit more about me — education, interests, and how I got here.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p>
      I'm Abdullakh, a Junior studying computer science at
      University of Houston. This site is where I keep track of what I'm building and write down
      things before I forget them.
    </p>

    <h2>Education</h2>
    <p>
   I'm working toward a B.S. in Computer Science at the University of Houston, with plans to add Math as a double major or minor, graduating in 2028. Before transferring, I finished an A.A.S. at Bergen Community College in New Jersey, where I did a research internship and competed in hackathons, including a quantum computing hackathon. Before that I was in Kazakhstan, at Bilim Innovation Lyceum (BIL), mostly focused on math olympiads.
    </p>
    <p>
      College so far has taught me to be more socially active without losing track of my priorities. What I like most is watching coursework turn into something applicable rather than staying abstract.

Courses I've taken: Data Structures & Algorithms, Computer Organization & Assembly Language, Advanced Programming Concepts, Object-Oriented Programming, Discrete Math, Intro to Logic, Calculus I & II, Physics I & II, Linear Algebra, Statistics.
    </p>

    <h2>What I'm into</h2>
    <p>
      Outside of class I hike, box, and play soccer and basketball. Most weekends I'm at the gym or with my brothers.
    </p>

    {
      photos.length > 1 ? (
        <div class="photo-row">
          {photos.map((photo) => (
            <figure class="photo">
              <Image src={photo.src} alt={photo.alt} width={640} />
              {photo.caption && <figcaption>{photo.caption}</figcaption>}
            </figure>
          ))}
        </div>
      ) : (
        <figure class="photo photo-single">
          <Image src={photos[0].src} alt={photos[0].alt} width={640} />
          {photos[0].caption && <figcaption>{photos[0].caption}</figcaption>}
        </figure>
      )
    }

    <h2>A bit of personality</h2>
    <p>
      coming soon...
    </p>

    <p>
      If any of this resonates (or you just want to talk), reach out — my email's in the
      <a href="/">footer</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .photo-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .photo img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 240px;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .photo figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--space-1);
  }

  .photo-single {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    width: min(320px, 100%);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  @media (max-width: 48em) {
    .photo-row {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 30em) {
    .photo-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
